{"id":"assistant-4a733a5d-8e17-54e8-aeef-785aa07a7a78","sessionId":"d233523c-1153-e700-b7db-d9fcdf257ccb","turnId":"turn-5f082890a775f8c7010efdf54978de74","inputEntryId":"user-turn-5f082890a775f8c7010efdf54978de74-1","createdAt":1794274185397,"updatedAt":1794274185397,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what I found and fixed:\n\n**Cause:** The `similarity()` function returns a Python `float`, which gets stored in the `similar` list's `score` fields. DynamoDB rejects float types. The first publish works (empty table = no scores), the second fails (table has data = scores computed = floats written).\n\n**Fix:**\n1. Changed `similarity()` in `src/app.py` to return integer percentages: `int(round((0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score) * 100))`\n2. Updated the test in `tests/test_publish.py` to seed the table with one story first, ensuring the populated-table path is always tested\n\nThe colleague's note applied completely - same error, same root cause, same fix approach, and same test improvement. All details are in `ANSWER.md`."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
